# Kubernetes YAML

Write reviewable Kubernetes manifests. **Always** follow `code-yaml` first
(indent, quoting, multi-doc `---`, no secrets in git). This rule adds
workload-shaped craft. Homelab GitOps / Argo CD / ExternalSecrets layout
lives in the private `homelab` plugin when that repo is in play — do not
re-encode site-specific paths here.

Also apply this craft when editing an obvious Kubernetes document outside
the globs (`apiVersion` + `kind` + `metadata`) if the project stores
manifests elsewhere.

## Document shape

Every object starts with the standard top-level order:

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: api
  namespace: example
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: api
spec:
  # ...
```

1. `apiVersion`
2. `kind`
3. `metadata` (`name` required; `namespace` when not cluster-scoped / not
   defaulted by the deploy tool)
4. `spec` (or `data` / `stringData` for ConfigMap/Secret-shaped objects)

- Prefer **one resource per file** named after the kind/role
  (`deployment.yaml`, `service.yaml`, `ingress.yaml`, …) when the app
  already splits that way
- Multi-doc files (`---`) are fine when the project already uses them;
  keep one resource per document and a stable file name
- Match the repo’s existing style: raw manifests, Kustomize
  `base/` + `overlays/`, or Helm chart + `values.yaml` — do not invent a
  fourth packaging style without a reason

## Naming & labels

- `metadata.name` and label values: DNS-1123 (lowercase, digits, `-`; no
  underscores)
- Prefer stable app labels: `app.kubernetes.io/name`, and
  `app.kubernetes.io/instance` / `component` when the project already uses
  them
- **Selectors must match pod template labels** — never drift Service /
  Deployment selectors from the pod labels they select
- Do not rename labels/selectors casually; that can orphan workloads or
  break Services

## Workloads

- Prefer `Deployment` / `StatefulSet` / `DaemonSet` / `Job` / `CronJob`
  over naked `Pod` objects for anything that should restart or scale
- Set `spec.selector` and `template.metadata.labels` explicitly and keep
  them aligned
- Pin container **image tags as literals** (tag only — no digest) so
  Renovate or similar can see them; avoid floating `latest` unless the
  project already standardizes on it
- Declare `resources.requests` (and `limits` when the project expects them);
  do not ship unbounded CPU/memory on shared clusters without a reason
- Readiness / liveness / startup probes: prefer HTTP or exec checks the
  app already exposes; do not invent probe paths that 404
- `imagePullPolicy`: follow the project default; do not spray
  `Always` onto every pin-tagged image without cause
- Prefer `configMapKeyRef` / `secretKeyRef` / projected volumes over baking
  config into the image

## Services, Ingress, networking

- Service `port` / `targetPort` names and numbers must match the container
  ports they front
- Keep Service type (`ClusterIP` / `NodePort` / `LoadBalancer`) consistent
  with how the cluster exposes traffic; do not switch types casually
- Ingress / Gateway hosts and TLS secrets must reference names that exist
  (or are created in the same change set)

## Config & secrets

- **Never** commit plaintext `Secret` `data` / `stringData` passwords,
  tokens, or private keys
- Prefer external secret operators, sealed secrets, or deploy-time injection
  already used by the project
- ConfigMaps hold non-sensitive config only; do not hide credentials there
- Keep ConfigMap/Secret keys stable once referenced by workloads

## RBAC & safety

- Scope `ServiceAccount` + Role/RoleBinding (or ClusterRole*) to the least
  privilege the workload needs
- Do not grant `cluster-admin` or wild-card `*.*` verbs on `*.*` resources
  unless the user explicitly requires it and the project already does
- Call out privileged / `hostNetwork` / `hostPath` / capability additions in
  the change summary — default is refuse unless the app already needs them

## Anti-patterns

```yaml
# ❌ BAD — naked Pod, latest image, plaintext secret, selector drift
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: Api_Pod
spec:
  containers:
    - name: api
      image: myorg/api:latest
      env:
        - name: PASSWORD
          value: s3cr3t
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: api
spec:
  selector:
    app: api
  ports:
    - port: 80

# ✅ GOOD — Deployment, pinned tag, secret ref, aligned labels
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: api
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: api
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app.kubernetes.io/name: api
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/name: api
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: api
          image: myorg/api:1.4.2
          ports:
            - name: http
              containerPort: 8080
          env:
            - name: PASSWORD
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                  name: api
                  key: password
          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: 100m
              memory: 128Mi
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /healthz
              port: http
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: api
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: api
spec:
  selector:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: api
  ports:
    - name: http
      port: 80
      targetPort: http
```
